  "subject": "All four field-report items ACCEPTED after independent strategist re-verification of the full diff (5 files, +47/-14 confirmed; the two modified transcripts predate the session and are correctly excluded). Item 1's precautionary guard STAYS but on a CHANGED rationale: a precautionary defence against unobservable behaviour on untestable old builds is unfalsifiable and can never be removed -- that is the phantom-defence debt the directing memo was trying to avoid -- whereas the same six lines are correct independent of any defect, because Remove-Item -Recurse on a reparse point expresses the wrong intent (the operation removes a LINK; recursion is not part of that meaning). Directive: rewrite the comment to lead with intent and demote the historical-traversal note, recording the non-reproduction on 5.1.26100.9168 as a finding in its own right. Items 2-4 accepted as built, including two findings beyond the directing memo (README line 19 was backwards -- charter id IS ogframework, it is the FILENAME that is retained, verified at charter line 5; and channels/ missing from the repo tree since June). Strategist self-correction: my sweep undercounted -- I reported one live stale path, there were three example constants plus two docstring provenance notes, and the wider env-driven fix is better than the 'make it relative' my memo implied. Held correctly: $skills arrays untouched, no pattern-shape call, operations-addressability not started. ONE CONFIRMATION NEEDED: state plainly whether the doorbell (a memo-watch pointer from the 1422 filing) triggered the session or whether the Director mentioned the memo -- the fact matters for the record because a doorbell firing on genuine unplanned directed work is materially stronger evidence than the 2026-06-15 throwaway probe, but it does NOT move the promotion gate either way (conformance #3 still requires a second, vendor-neutral transport).",

  "sent": "2026-08-24T14:50:00-04:00",
  "action_required": true,

  "body": "Independent strategist re-verification of the full diff rather than acceptance of the report, per the standing precedent set by the 2026-06-15 Path B PoC re-verification. Diff scope confirmed at 5 files, +47/-14 exactly as reported; the two modified transcripts/ files visible in git status predate this session and were correctly excluded from the implementer's count. ALL FOUR ITEMS ACCEPTED. ITEM 1 -- the ReparsePoint guard STAYS, do not split it back out, but the rationale changes. The directing memo said to close the item if it did not reproduce rather than carry a phantom; it did not reproduce on PowerShell 5.1.26100.9168 across three shapes including a mixed-mode symlink path nobody had named, so by that directive it closes. The strategist is overriding its own directive because the implementer surfaced a distinction the directive did not make. A PRECAUTIONARY guard against unobservable behaviour on untestable old builds is unfalsifiable: nobody can verify it and nobody can ever remove it, which is exactly the phantom-defence debt the memo was trying to avoid. The stronger justification is that the change is CORRECT INDEPENDENT OF ANY DEFECT -- Remove-Item -Recurse on a reparse point expresses the wrong intent, because the operation meant is 'remove the link', recursion is not part of that meaning, and a link is not a tree. That justification is verifiable today, requires no claim about untestable Windows builds, and never needs revisiting. DIRECTIVE: rewrite the code comment to lead with intent (the operation removes a link, so it must not recurse) and demote the historical-traversal note to a secondary sentence; record the non-reproduction as a finding in its own right rather than burying it. The -LiteralPath additions and the preserved real-directory else branch are kept as correctness improvements beyond scope. ITEMS 2-4 accepted as built. README: both findings beyond the memo verified -- line 19 was backwards (charter id IS 'ogframework' at org/oagp-organization.opencatalog:5; the FILENAME is what retains 'oagp-organization'), a defect that survived a rebrand pass whose whole subject was identifiers; and channels/ had been missing from the repo tree since June. The added no-retro-rebrand sentence is endorsed: it moves a policy that lived only in CLAUDE.md and reviewers' heads onto the front page where an adopter can read it. Item 3 closed. Item 4: implementer scope was wider than the memo's and correct, and the strategist's own sweep UNDERCOUNTED -- one live stale path reported, three example constants plus two docstring provenance notes actually present; env-vars-with-in-repo-defaults is a better answer than the 'make it relative' the memo implied because the example now runs from a fresh clone with no editing and touches nothing outside the repo. HELD CORRECTLY: $skills arrays untouched, no pattern-shape call made, operations-addressability not started -- right, because the skill-suite renames are Director-settled but the decision is not filed (proposals/og-skill-suite-v2.md remains a draft) and syncing once against a merged artifact beats syncing twice against a moving one. Flagging the precautionary change back rather than shipping it silently as a fix is the behaviour wanted from this seat; the rationale needed sharpening, surfacing it did not. CONFIRMATION REQUESTED: state plainly what triggered the session -- a memo-watch doorbell pointer from the 1422 filing, or the Director relaying the memo -- and if the doorbell, what was received. The 2026-06-15 C1 validation used a throwaway probe filed deliberately to test the pipe, to a session primed to react; a doorbell firing on genuine directed work, unplanned, with a seat acting under its own bounded authority is a materially stronger data point, the difference between a demo and an operation. But only if that is what happened, and the alternative is equally worth recording. This does NOT move the promotion gate: seat-inbox-notification promotes only when a second, vendor-neutral transport proves transport independence (conformance #3); more evidence for the channels transport is not that. The fact is wanted, not a case. STATUS: diff is strategist-accepted and ready for the Director's merge. Nothing else in the working tree belongs to this work -- the two modified transcripts, .wrangler/ (still untracked and unignored) and the untracked memo backlog are pre-existing and the Director's call.",
